        "title": "Hindu culture to the extreme",
        "text": "This was my 2nd visit to Pashupatinath where I introduced my sister to this unbelievable site. First of all, non-Hindus are prohibited from entering their temple, but there's plenty to experience in the environs. Many foreigners are a bit shocked to see the non-stop cremations burning along the river, but they do make for some interesting photos. Beware of the non-stop stream of \"local guides\" who will nag you to death. This site does not require a long stay and we were happy to move on to Boudanath and Swayambhuath for a more relaxed Buddhist cultural experience.",
